---
/**
 * Privacy. Short, accurate, and written to match what this site actually does —
 * which at present is very little, because a static build with no client
 * JavaScript collects nothing on its own.
 *
 * This page gets rewritten the moment analytics or a third-party widget ships.
 * A privacy page that describes a site you no longer run is worse than none.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { BUSINESS } from '../data/business';
import { buildTitle } from '../lib/seo';

export const prerender = true;
const updated = '2026-09-15';

const schema = {
  path: '/privacy/',
  title: buildTitle('Privacy'),
  description: 'What King of Kings Window Cleaning collects on this website, what it does not collect, and how to ask us about the information we hold.',
  image: '/brand/king-of-kings-social.jpg',
  imageAlt: 'Privacy information for King of Kings Window Cleaning',
  crumbs: [{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy/' }],
  faqs: [],
};
---
<BaseLayout schema={schema} noindex={true}>
  <article class="t1 prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>

    <h2>What this site collects</h2>
    <p>
      This website is a set of static pages. It has no login, cart or account, and
      the pages themselves collect nothing about you.
    </p>

    <h2>The chat widget</h2>
    <p>
      Most pages carry a chat widget provided by LeadConnector, which is the
      messaging tool behind our customer relationship system. It loads after the
      page has rendered — when you first scroll, tap or type, or shortly after if
      you do none of those — rather than immediately, and it is not present on the
      contact or guarantee pages.
    </p>
    <p>
      When it loads it runs LeadConnector's own code and will set its own storage
      in your browser so a conversation survives a page change. If you start a
      chat, what you type goes to LeadConnector and to us, and we use it to answer
      you and to quote the work. LeadConnector processes it under its own terms as
      our provider.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you would rather not load it, it will not start on its own before you
      interact with the page, and blocking third-party scripts in your browser
      stops it entirely — the rest of the site works without it, because nothing
      on these pages depends on JavaScript.
    </p>

    <h2>What happens when you contact us</h2>
    <p>
      If you call, email, or submit a quote request, we keep what you send us —
      your name, contact details, the address of the property and what you have
      asked about — so we can quote and carry out the work. We use it for that and
      for following up about it. We do not sell it.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served by our hosting provider, which keeps standard server logs
      including IP addresses for security and operational purposes. That is the
      provider's processing, not ours, and it is the ordinary behaviour of any web
      server.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Where we link out — to our Google Business Profile, to a review platform, to
      a quote form hosted elsewhere — that service has its own privacy terms and
      its own cookies, and following the link puts you under those rather than
      these. If we later add analytics, this page will say so before it ships and
      will name what it is — as it does above for the chat widget.
    </p>

    <h2>Asking about your information</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.email}`}>{BUSINESS.email}</a> or call{' '}
      <a href={`tel:${BUSINESS.phoneE164}`}>{BUSINESS.phone}</a> and ask. We will
      tell you what we hold and remove it if you want it removed.
    </p>

    <p class="updated">Last updated <time datetime={updated}>{updated}</time>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
